* Randomness on Aztec
** One oracle
*** aztec::oracle::random::random()
*** oracle attribute aztec_misc_getRandomField
*** PXE / TXE: Fr.random()
*** 64 CSPRNG bytes mod r
*** SEED env = deterministic (tests only)
** Four framework uses
*** Note blinding H(owner, r)
*** Private event commitment
*** Ephemeral encryption key
*** Ciphertext padding
*** + fallback tag, client salts and nonces
** Three values in a note
*** r: client, blinds the hash
*** nonce: protocol, H(first_nullifier, index), unique
*** nullifier: owner's nsk_app, marks the spend
** Unconstrained by design
*** Chooser already knows the preimage
*** Constraint would protect against nothing
*** Consistency is what the circuit checks
*** Bad r weakens privacy, never ownership
** Limits
*** No oracle in public functions
*** No beacon or VRF: privacy, not fairness
*** Partial note: one draw, one use
*** Reuse links payments, loses the second
@endmindmap
